WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.458
Foreign keys also need a decision about what happens
when a parent

00:00:03.471 --> 00:00:09.175
row is deleted RESTRICT or NO ACTION blocks the
deletion while dependent

00:00:09.188 --> 00:00:13.862
child rows exist This is often appropriate for
master data such as

00:00:13.888 --> 00:00:20.533
patients providers or services that are referenced
by historical activity CASCADE

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:25.851
automatically removes dependent child rows That can
be appropriate when the child

00:00:25.878 --> 00:00:29.562
has no meaning without the parent such as
appointment service lines when

00:00:29.575 --> 00:00:35.010
the appointment itself is deleted SET NULL keeps the
child but removes

00:00:35.036 --> 00:00:40.452
the reference which only makes sense when the
relationship is optional Do

00:00:40.466 --> 00:00:45.666
not choose CASCADE simply because it is convenient
Choose the referential action

00:00:45.692 --> 00:00:49.403
based on the real meaning and retention requirements
of the relationship
